X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_ashevillehikinggroup
X-SOURCE:Asheville Hiking Group
UID:event_314885901@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260524T041427Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260526T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260526T200000
SUMMARY:Scenic AVL #9 - Downtown to Windswept from First Baptist Church
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Meeting Place:** Park in the Fir
 st Baptist Church parking lot between the church and the YMCA.\n**Meeting 
 Point:** [https://maps.app.goo.gl/zYYZFLSk7rg4pdrP6](https://maps.app.goo.
 gl/zYYZFLSk7rg4pdrP6)\n**Rating:** Strenuous for Pace and Distance\n**Surf
 ace:** Road and some trail\n**Mileage:** about 5.5 miles\n**Elevation Gain
 :** 750\n**Sun Exposure: This is a mostly urban hike\, about 30% shade.**\
 n**Pace:** 3.0 mph flats\, slower on steep climbs. We will stop at the top
  of Windswept for a short break\, and we will finish within 2 hours. We wa
 lk at a pretty fast pace\, so please be aware of your capabilities.\n**Fea
 tures:** Downtown points of interest\, views from Windswept. Bears rarely 
 seen.\n**After Eats:** Taco Temple\n**Dogs: Well behaved dogs are welcome.
  Bring water - it's gets hot on the climb!**\n\n**Scenic Asheville Series:
 ** There are 10 hikes in the [series](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1
 1ewlUM9OV8I4npc1cNNsSYOnXI0QPw2isAleXdFzEbI/edit?usp=drivesdk)\; hike 9 of
  them and receive an attractive [badge](https://docs.google.com/drawings/d
 /1goXUXfzUBqhB4_UeCxodlk4ZPeCCgqZrWK2EUJvk_vI/edit) for your backpack. Che
 ck your progress [HERE](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1XUm-X1_Ohx
 KIi8JU5rhjsW37cAl4yYx8yB_NEjjI5Lk/edit?usp=sharing). Check out our highlig
 hts [here](https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/18cFp2Uhw8XthOFXxekBpt2L
 GP6ww-V7kmXQExI7Y0h0/edit?usp=drivesdk).\n\n**General Route:** [Avl Urban 
 Trail to Windswept](https://www.alltrails.com/explore/map/evening-hike-at-
 avl-urban-trail-to-windswept-7949e45)\nHere is the full list of waypoints\
 , but we will not stop for all of them: [Downtown to Windswept Waypoints](
 https://docs.google.com/document/d/1h6VbzxQjBE8Ha6X8kfX9Hhtvn9LE-Q5BgD_Uz1
 2SE-c/edit?usp=sharing)\n\nRSVP and On-Time Start:\n\n*If you decide you c
 annot come\, please change your RSVP\, so that Wait-listers can move up.\n
 - There are generally 1 or 2 no-shows on my hikes\, so we don't wait for p
 eople to arrive. If you are late\, you'll be left behind.\n*Notes and comm
 ents are genuinely appreciated.\n\n**Guests**: Please make sure your guest
 s know the distance\, pace and elevation gain.\n\n**Disclaimer and Release
  of Liability:**\nThis activity involves hiking on city streets that may h
 ave traffic. Participants are responsible for their safety on streets and 
 trails. The organizer of this trip is a volunteer and not a professional g
 uide. The function of the organizer is only to organize this trip. If you 
 sign up or participate in this event you acknowledge that you freely and v
 oluntarily agree to assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, and damages
  arising from\, as a result of\, and associated with this event. In additi
 on\, you acknowledge that you agree to the Meetup terms: [https://www.meet
 up.com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/terms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/314885901
 /
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260521T015658Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260521T015658Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Shutupandwriteasheville": "https://www.meetup.com/shutupandwriteasheville/events/314666318/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_shutupandwriteasheville
X-SOURCE:Shut Up & Write Western NC
UID:event_314666318@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260524T043219Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260526T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260526T193000
SUMMARY:Shut Up & Write!® - Downtown
DESCRIPTION:Shut Up & Write!® Western North Carolina\n***\\*\\*\\*Please 
 note: event listings are moving to the Shut Up & Write! website and this M
 eetup page will be closed in a few weeks. You will find our Tuesday night 
 events here: [https://www.shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00](https://www
 .shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00)\\*\\*\\****\n\n**Here's how it works
 .** Show up at or before 6:00. At 6:00\, we do some quick introductions. A
 fterward\, for a full 60 minutes (I'll set a timer!) we are heads-down wri
 ting. Writing what? A novel? You bet. Some poetry? Sure. Song lyrics? Your
  resume? That report you need to get to your boss before 8 AM or you'll *n
 eed* *to write* that resume? All of the above and more. Just shut up and w
 rite.\n\nSurrounding ourselves with other writers who are busy putting wor
 ds onto page (physical or virtual) keeps us all accountable and focused.\n
 \nWhen the timer goes off\, we'll check-in with each other and see how it 
 went. Afterward\, feel free to stay to chat and get to know your fellow wr
 iters\, or keep writing\, or take off.\n\nSocializing is optional and will
  happen after (or briefly before) the focused writing. This is a safe spac
 e to work on your craft. No one will read or critique your writing.\n\nFor
  more information about our events\, visit [https://shutupwrite.com](https
 ://shutupwrite.com).\n\n**What to Expect**\n\n* Roughly 15 minutes of intr
 oductions\n* 60 minutes of focused writing (somebody set a timer)!\n* Afte
 rward\, optional socializing\n\n**Being late is okay:** Just show up and g
 et settled\, then check in with the host after the session. (Look for the 
 person with the Shut Up & Write sign).\n\n**What Should I Bring?**\n\n* Wh
 atever you need to be able to write!\n* Earbuds/earplugs if you want to bl
 ock ambient noise.\n\n**Other Important Details:**\n\n***\\*\\*\\*Please n
 ote: event listings are moving to the Shut Up & Write! website and this Me
 etup page will be closed in a few weeks. You will find our Tuesday night e
 vents here: [https://www.shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00](https://www.
 shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00)\\*\\*\\****\n\nHOSTS: This is a multi
 -host event\, so most of the time there will be a host present. If we are 
 unlucky and no host can attend\, please find each other and self-organize.
  Pay attention to the event chat and comments to see who is available.\n\n
 WI-FI: Yes!\n\nPARKING: Street parking in metered spots is free after 6pm.
  Closest municipal garages ($2/hour) are Wall St. & Coxe Street/Sears Alle
 y.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/shutupandwriteasheville/events/314666
 318/
