BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Meetup Group Ssbjicnx": "https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-ssbjicnx/events/bnlxwtyjcjbxb/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_meetup_group_ssbjicnx
X-SOURCE:Dodgeball AVL
UID:event_bnlxwtyjcjbxb@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260524T043215Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260618T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260618T220000
SUMMARY:Dodgeball Open Play (ages 21+)
DESCRIPTION:Dodgeball AVL\n**This is an outdoor event so weather can affec
 t our Meetup. We do not play in rain\, temps below 40F\, or other adverse 
 weather conditions. Keep on eye on the weather and check group updates to 
 stay informed. ** Waitlisted players\, please still consider attending! 
 We only sit players if games have reached capacity. That’s 12v12 for one
  court and 11v11 for 2 courts. We usually have less people at the beginnin
 g after setup (~7:15pm) and the end of the night (after 9pm). That said\, 
 we are growing in attendance so play time is not guaranteed for the waitli
 st and those who do not sign up. Ready to dodge\, duck\, dip\, dive\, an
 d dodge? Come show us what you got with Asheville’s weekly pick-up dodge
 ball group! We're hosting open play on Thursday night at Asheville Sport
 s Club. We are all about having a great time and getting that adrenaline p
 umping! Friendly competition is always welcome but fun\, safety\, and resp
 ect for all players are the top priorities. We use squishy rubber dodgebal
 ls that are fun to throw and catch but can sting with enough velocity so n
 o headshots are allowed. Throws should aim at your target’s shoulders or
  lower. No experience is necessary - we'll teach you the rules. Open to 
 adults 21 and up (bring your ID!). We’re sorry but we cannot accommodate
  teens or children because there is alcohol on the premises and no one wan
 ts to be the person who accidentally hurts a kid. Sign waivers at the bar 
 before playing and enjoy a beverage between games. Rules of the game are
  covered at the start of the event so please be there at 7pm to learn our 
 format. We loosely follow the USA Dodgeball ruleset with some exceptions t
 o help new players adapt to the game more quickly. Check out our brief rul
 es and expectations summary attached as photos to this Meetup. Here’s 
 an approximate schedule for this event depending on when people arrive: 
 6:50 - 7:10pm* - Set up courts and mingle - help with set up is appreciate
 d! 7:10 - 7:15pm - Rules and announcements 7:15 - 9:30pm - Play! *If
  we have enough people once setup is done\, we’ll jump into rules and an
 nouncements early. We need at least 8 players to start a game\, so take ad
 vantage of the daylight and try to arrive right at the beginning! Since 
 this is a free event\, the more community support we can gather\, the bett
 er experience everyone will have\, especially for the organizers! If you'd
  like to help\, please arrive early or stay late to assist with set up and
  breakdown. This is a free community offering\, however\, if you are fee
 ling generous\, donations are welcomed to help support and expand our grou
 p. We take donations through Pledge here in Meetup or Venmo (dodgeballavl)
 . Cash of course is great too and more effective as there are no platform 
 fees. Your donations genuinely help the group by helping with equipment pu
 rchases and raising funds to eventually add another night of dodgeball in 
 an indoor gym. This event would not be possible without the support of Ash
 eville Sports Club. Please consider generously tipping your bartenders and
  karaoke DJ as well.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-ssbjicnx/events/bnlxwtyj
 cjbxb/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260411T152140Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260411T152140Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-appalachian-arts-crafts-rising-6th-8th-grade/2026-06-19/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260619
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260620
DTSTAMP:20260524T001426
CREATED:20260127T202635Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260513T210106Z
UID:10006625-1781827200-1781913599@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:Summer Art Camp | Appalachian Arts & Crafts (Rising 6th - 8th grade)
DESCRIPTION:REGISTER HERE \nBlending creativity with cultural heritage\, students will explore the artistic traditions of Appalachian culture through a series of hands-on crafts. They will begin the week creating vibrant painted barn quilts and learning basic weaving techniques with natural materials. They’ll spend the remainder of the week further developing their weaving skills to make reed baskets and needle felting a landscape.   \nMeet the Instructor: Kati Robbins\nKati Robbins has over 12 years of experience as an art educator\, teaching studio arts and crafts to a wide range of age groups in different learning environments. She is currently based in Asheville where she works as a high school art teacher. Her creative work focuses on mixed media and assemblage\, with a strong interest in collaborative and community based projects. She is inspired by Appalachian craft traditions\, natural materials and the surrounding landscape. When Kati isn’t teaching or making art\, she enjoys gardening\, cooking\, reading and hiking in the mountains. 
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-appalachian-arts-crafts-rising-6th-8th-grade/2026-06-19/
LOCATION:Asheville Art Museum\, 2 South Pack Square\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:Summer Art Camp
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/1976.62.71_New-1.jpg
GEO:35.5946714;-82.5512827
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Asheville Art Museum 2 South Pack Square Asheville NC 28801 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=2 South Pack Square:geo:-82.5512827,35.5946714
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-ancient-to-modern-mixed-media-traditions-reimagined-rising-6th-8th-grade/2026-06-19/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260619
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260620
DTSTAMP:20260524T001426
CREATED:20260127T203717Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260513T210013Z
UID:10006620-1781827200-1781913599@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:Summer Art Camp | Ancient to Modern: Mixed Media Traditions Reimagined (Rising 6th - 8th grade)
DESCRIPTION:REGISTER HERE \nThroughout history\, artists have experimented with wax\, fabric\, pigment\, metal\, and glass to create expressive and symbolic artworks. In this camp\, we’ll explore how ancient art-making techniques like batik\, encaustic\, and gilded mosaics can inspire new creative directions. Students will work hands-on with traditional materials and reinterpret them through a contemporary lens\, experimenting with resists\, mixed-media layering\, transparency\, and texture.  \nMeet the Instructor: Kristina Shriver\nKristina Shriver is a visual art educator with over 16 years of experience\, working with students of all ages. She teaches at Asheville High School and serves as an AP Studio Art Reader and mentor for other art educators. Kristina designs hands-on\, material-rich art experiences that connect historical techniques to contemporary practice\, emphasizing experimentation\, personal storytelling\, and meaningful creative exploration.   
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-ancient-to-modern-mixed-media-traditions-reimagined-rising-6th-8th-grade/2026-06-19/
LOCATION:Asheville Art Museum\, 2 South Pack Square\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:Summer Art Camp
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/2000.27.72.jpg
GEO:35.5946714;-82.5512827
